{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-truth-panel-pay-machines-b-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"gap-9","surface":"panel","area":"panel/pay-machines","refs":["F-panel-107","F-panel-1104"],"severity":"S3","title":"All branches lists people whose plan ended longest ago first, and cuts the newest off","what":"On All branches, 'Who to call, in every branch', the list 'Plan ended (last 30 days)' is sorted so the member who lapsed 30 days ago comes first and yesterday's lapse comes last. The list stops at 60 names with 'And N more'. A gym group with many lapses loses exactly the people most worth calling. Every other list in the admin app puts the most recent lapse first.","expected":"Most recently ended first, the same order as the member lists, so the cut-off drops the oldest lapses.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/branches/logic.ts:252","apps/dashboard/src/crm/branches/logic.ts:256-260","apps/dashboard/src/crm/branches/AllBranches.tsx:30","apps/dashboard/src/crm/branches/AllBranches.tsx:176","apps/dashboard/src/crm/branches/AllBranches.tsx:195-196","apps/dashboard/src/crm/logic/membership.ts:455-470"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"ended-list-sorted-oldest-first","who":"owners with more than one branch","how_often":"every time the ended list is opened","fix_line":"Sort the ended list with the newest lapse first, as the other lists do","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
